## Safety (delete if this ADR does not touch actuation — spec §11)

{Answer each that applies; "n/a" is an answer, silence is not.
- Rungs 1–8: read-only default? who confirms the first write? may-disturb warnings in the
  action manifest? interlock (a lease, no force door)? exception-safe restore? refusals
  in-band? independent kill for safety-critical TX?
- Rung 9 — the single writer: which code is the ONLY writer, and where the safety
  properties are enforced.
- Rung 10 — the ownership door: how non-owner acts are recorded as requests.
- Rung 11 — dead-man level: what is held safe, the declared cadence, the derived timeout.
- Rung 12 — does this remove or weaken a safety behaviour? Name the replacement and the
  confinement (flag / scenario) until it ships.
- Rung 13 — which consumers enforce the safety predicate, from which canonical authority.
- Constants: each behaviour/safety number links to its ledger entry (§8.11).}

